p2-windows/W7 — page:settings/ActiveSessions — native WinUI 3 ActiveSessionsPage at web parity
================================================================================================
Web source : web/src/features/settings/pages/ActiveSessionsPage.tsx
             (+ the wrapped web/src/features/settings/components/ActiveSessionsSection.tsx)
Web route  : /account/sessions  (nav name "Active Sessions")
Output     : apps/windows/TeslaSync.App/feature-views/ActiveSessionsPage/{ActiveSessionsPage.cs,
             ActiveSessionsPage.Model.cs, ActiveSessionsPage.Source.cs, ActiveSessionsPage.ViewModel.cs}
             (real in-repo path; the generated prompt's apps/windows/TeslaSync/Features/Settings path
              does not exist — the Windows app is TeslaSync.App with C#-markup feature-views, not
              XAML-per-page, and the platform string catalog lives at apps/windows/Strings/*.resw.
              This mirrors every prior W7 page in apps/parity/windows-ledger.json.)

Shape of the parity unit
------------------------
The web page is a <PageContainer title subtitle copyLink> hosting <ActiveSessionsSection />. The manifest
record (apps/parity/parity-manifest.json id=page:settings/ActiveSessions) lists requiredCount=2, both
strings (account.sessions.title + account.sessions.subtitle) and NO data sources/panels/charts/maps of its
own. There is NO separate parity unit for ActiveSessionsSection, so — honouring "no scope narrowing / no
stubs as final" — the hosted section is reproduced natively in full (it is not stubbed): the four web render
branches (loading, open-mode AUTH_MODE_OPEN notice, forward-auth table, empty) plus the per-row Sign out and
the "Sign out all other devices" action, both behind a destructive, never-silenceable confirm dialog.

Native realisation (Fluent / WinUI 3, ADR-002/004/005/006/011)
--------------------------------------------------------------
- ActiveSessionsPage : UserControl — mounts the shared PageContainer surface (parity port of web
  PageContainer, apps/windows/TeslaSync.App/shared-surfaces/PageContainer.cs) with CopyLink=true and
  PageContent = a Fluent TsGlassPanel whose body switches between the loading notice (Spinner + caption),
  the open-mode notice (Warning glyph + PanelTitle + HelperText), the failure surface (TsErrorDisplay +
  Retry) and the forward-auth panel (header with the all-others TsButton, the sessions table with a
  "this device" TsBadge + a per-row Sign out TsButton, or the empty Text). Revokes confirm through
  TsConfirmDialog (IsDestructive=true). Design tokens + a11y (AutomationProperties, Group peer) throughout.
- ActiveSessionsPageViewModel : INotifyPropertyChanged — UI-thread-free state holder. Reads the list
  through IActiveSessionsFeed (web useSessions); owns the per-row + all-others revoke flows (web
  useRevokeSession / useRevokeAllOtherSessions); projects ActiveSessionsDisplay so the view is a thin
  renderer. LoadAsync/RefreshAsync + RevokeAsync/RevokeAllOthersAsync; superseding CTS; no I/O in the view.
- ActiveSessionsProjection / ActiveSessionsModel / ActiveSessionsDisplay — pure projection (no WinUI types)
  resolving the five-state matrix (loading / open-mode / error / empty / populated), the device-label
  heuristic (1:1 port of web describeDevice), the timestamp cells (shared SI/locale DateTimeFormatting),
  the "this device" chip + per-row revoke affordance, and the two destructive confirm-copy templates.
- ActiveSessionsSnapshot.FromJson — tolerant list parser ({mode,sessions} object, {data:[…]} envelope,
  bare array; explicit mode:'open' -> open snapshot). ActiveSessionsRegistration — RouteName="ActiveSessions"
  (matches RouteTable.cs Page("ActiveSessions","account/sessions",SettingsAccountIntegrations)),
  Slug="ActiveSessionsPage", the three generated operation ids (get_api_v1_auth_sessions,
  delete_api_v1_auth_sessions_id, delete_api_v1_auth_sessions_all_others) + AUTH_MODE_OPEN sentinel.
- EmptyActiveSessionsFeed — the no-backend default the parameterless (shell-registered) page hosts itself
  against (resolved-but-empty forward-auth list -> empty state), mirroring the other W7 pages' Empty feeds.
  ActiveSessionsClientFeed — the generated-OpenAPI-client adapter (ADR-004): GET + the two DELETEs, mapping
  the 501 AUTH_MODE_OPEN to the open snapshot exactly as web useSessions does.
- Shell registration: apps/windows/TeslaSync.App/Shell/ShellWindow.xaml.cs registers
  PageFactory.Register("ActiveSessions", () => new FeatureViews.Settings.ActiveSessionsPage()).
  (Same edit also closed a pre-existing merge artifact in the Locations registration lambda that left the
   constructor unbalanced — CS1026/CS1002/CS1513 at ShellWindow.xaml.cs:251 — which had the whole App
   project red on arrival; required to reach a green BUILD gate.)

Faithful-improvement note (data states / ADR-011)
-------------------------------------------------
The web maps a genuinely-errored list query to the open-mode branch (its `!sessions.data` guard catches the
undefined data). The native surface instead promotes a real list-load failure to a dedicated error+Retry
state (the prompt's "error -> InfoBar + Retry; never render a blank region" contract), while the explicit
501 AUTH_MODE_OPEN still resolves to the open-mode notice exactly as web. No branch is dropped or stubbed.

i18n note (R3/ADR-014)
----------------------
account.sessions.title / .subtitle (the two manifest strings) — and the hosted section's sessions.* keys
ported beyond the manifest minimum for full fidelity — are NOT catalog entries in either the web i18n source
or the generated platform catalog (apps/windows/Strings/{en,ar,he}/Resources.resw); the web resolves them as
inline t(key, default) fallbacks. The native surface resolves them the same way: keyed
ILocalizer.GetString(key, <same English default>) flowing through ShellLocalizer -> shell Localization
(resw lookup -> English fallback). Zero hardcoded literals; the auto-generated resw is left untouched (it is
machine-generated from web i18n; hand-editing would strand drift).

